-- title:
--   Special-fibre point of the j-finite chart over s, q=2
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $q=2$, a nonzero $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g\mid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a nonunit of $A$, and let $W$ be a finset of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$, the subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)$ generated over the residue field by the $j$-series $\mathrm{jqModC}$ and its substitution $q\mapsto q^{M'}$, whose members are exactly the supersingular places, i.e. the rational places $w$ satisfying `IsAffineGeomPlace` with $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen})\in\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q$; let $s\in W$. Assume $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'\le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, and let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ (the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change of the full level-$M'$ modular function field) with values in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$, assumed compatible with coefficientwise reduction: every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose image in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Let $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ with $\pi_0\in A$; write $A_0=A\cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$), and assume $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal $(\pi_0)$, henselian local, with algebraically closed residue field, and that every $a\in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some $c\in k_0\cap A$. Let $H_1=\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'\cap\ker\bigl((\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times\bigr)$, and let $K$ be the intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,k_0$ over $k_0$ generated by the coefficientwise images of $\mathrm{xHFunctionField}\,(q^2M')\,H_1$, equipped with an $A_0$-algebra structure compatible with $k_0$. Let $j\in K$ be nonzero with underlying Laurent series $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,k_0\,\mathrm{jq}$, and assume that this same series lies in $K$ and that the resulting element lies in $C=\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_0\,K\,j$, the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A_0[j]$. Then there is a maximal ideal $y$ of $C$ containing the image of $\pi_0$ such that for every $g\in\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb Q$ lying in the full level-$M'$ modular function field and whose image in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, subject to the conditions that $\mathrm{ord}_P(g)\ge 0$ at every place $P$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which $\mathrm{ord}_P(\mathrm{jq})\ge 0$ and that the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$, one has: whenever $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,k_0\,g$ lies in $K$ with resulting element in $C$, and $c\in k_0$ with $c\in A$ has residue in $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ equal to $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference of $g$ and the image of $c$ in $C$ lies in $y$.
--
--   This supplies, in the diamond-level frame at $q=2$, a point of the special fibre of the $j$-finite chart of the two-chart integral model of $X_{H_1}(q^2M')$ over $A_0$ which lies over the chosen supersingular place $s$ of the level-$M'$ reduction: the maximal ideal contains the uniformiser and separates no $s$-regular modular function from the constant given by its value at $s$. It is used by the refinement that in addition records supersingularity of the $j$-value at this point.
